{"reference":"Psalms 124","book":"Psalms","chapter":124,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"The Surrounding Psalms","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Psalm 124 stands among the Songs of Ascents, a surrounding collection oriented toward worship. In the wider collection, communal psalms remember experiences including sanctuary destruction and Babylonian exile, while other psalms voice thanksgiving for return, festival praise, and meditation on Torah. This broader setting is debated, but it helps situate Psalm 124's communal language of rescue within a collection that gives expression to shared worship and memory.","verse_refs":["Psalms 120:1-7","Psalms 121:1-8","Psalms 122:1-9","Psalms 123:1-4","Psalms 125:1-5","Psalms 126:1-6","Psalms 127:1-5","Psalms 128:1-6","Psalms 129:1-8","Psalms 130:1-8","Psalms 131:1-3","Psalms 132:1-18","Psalms 133:1-3","Psalms 134:1-3"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_psalms_124_b3d847ce3aacbc352be339ba"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}